WEBVTT

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:08.080
We can't get by with just
goods aimed at gatherers.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.080
I need to have more products
aimed at the villagers too,

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.000
if I want to stay open for business.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.710
Amazing!

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.670
Do you have any good ideas?

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.920
Things for the villagers, is it?

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.080
Well, this thing looks like it'd be great...

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.000
A water pump, huh?

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.710
But it uses quite a bit of magical power.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.290
How many houses even have
wells to begin with...?

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:41.170
Even including shared wells,
there aren't even ten.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.210
But they'd still be of use to everyone, huh?

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.330
Still, I'd prefer something a little simpler.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:51.250
Something simpler...

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:52.630
Ah!

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.250
It's already full!

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.500
Ow!

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:13.790
Starting today, I can see a small star

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:17.210
Shining bright in my heart

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.500
Whether crying, laughing, or shining

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.710
I'll roll up my sleeves and get walking

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:25.920
(It'll definitely be alright, give your worries the go sign)

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.170
(Let's do this right)

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:35.540
Being free can feel so restricting

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:38.880
After all, it never ends

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.290
This spiral of theoretical values and test results

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.420
Whether I win or lose

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:46.000
(No matter what I try)

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.670
I work hard to see my dream come true

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.500
(It's not a cheat, it's a life hack)

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.960
I've got the license to take my proper first step

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.210
This is just the beginning

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.460
Starting today, I can see a small star

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:02.830
Shining bright in my heart

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:06.210
Whether crying, laughing, or shining

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.790
I take a deep breath before work

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:12.960
Resound, as I reach out towards a whole new world

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.290
My dream is surely in my hands

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:19.710
An original only I can make

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:22.420
Open that door and say welcome

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.920
(This is the start)

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:28.460
(It'll definitely be alright, give your worries the go sign)

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.880
(Let's do this right)

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:35.250
Oww...

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.330
I got all distracted by the water pump...

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.460
The number of bugs around is
only going to keep growing,

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.000
so you take care too, Ms. Sarasa.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.130
That could work!

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:51.790
Spite worms?!

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.420
What are you going to use those for?

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:58.290
For now, I'm thinking of making
insect repellent veils.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:01.080
I feel like those would sell well with farmers.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.630
I see!

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.580
So, you want to have more goods like that!

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.040
Ms. Owner, we have returned!

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.130
Today, we brought back plast mushrooms.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.500
I see.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:18.790
It certainly would be hard to sell goods
aimed at gatherers to the villagers.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:20.380
Right?

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:21.710
Got it.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:25.130
We'll go ahead and actively try to
gather up some spite worms!

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:26.710
Thank you!

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:29.380
Hey Iris, are you listening properly?

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:33.040
Geez, go ahead and swallow first.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.170
My apologies!

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.920
Leave it to us, Ms. Owner!

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:44.080
Still, your cooking certainly has
gotten even tastier, Lorea!

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.460
That's because I've gotten used to
the magic stove and oven...

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:52.130
And of course, thanks to the
cook book from Ms. Sarasa.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:55.290
No, it's just down to how skilled you are!

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:59.830
Now if we could just get
a refrigerator and freezer...

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.960
A-a refrigerator?!

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:06.170
If you could preserve your ingredients,
it would make it easier to cook, right?

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:09.630
That's true, but that's such a high-class item...!

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:13.130
It won't be any issue if I make
the expensive cooling unit myself!

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:17.920
Well, it would be a bit of a hassle to use
a magical crystal for the cooling core,

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.830
but if I can use ice attribute ingredients
it shouldn't be so tough,

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:22.170
and would be a lot cheaper.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.790
If we ask for Mr. Geberk's help, we should
be able to handle the frames soon too.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.130
I see!

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:31.710
Are those ice attribute ingredients
something you could get ahold of soon?

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:36.790
Yes. For this area, I suppose it
would be frostfang bat fangs.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.580
Frostfang bats?

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.250
Have you heard of those, Iris?

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.540
I haven't heard of them either.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:51.040
Now that I think of it, I haven't had
any gatherers bring any in either...

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.830
They look like this.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:59.250
Frostfang bats...

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:02.040
I feel like I've heard of those somewhere...

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:04.000
Andre, are you thinking of that matter?

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.880
You know, what Mr. Drake told us way back!

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:10.290
Ah, those things living in the northern caves?

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:11.420
Yeah, that's it!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:15.420
In that case, we've never hunted them before.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:17.500
How strange.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:21.670
Frostfang bats are easy to hunt,
and to get ingredients from too...

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:27.330
From what we heard, when someone
brought those bats to South Straug

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:32.210
they were told they were unusable
and really had the price beaten down...

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:33.790
How strange...

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:39.170
Even unprocessed they shouldn't really
deteriorate, which makes them desirable...

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:43.670
No way... So, they were tricked?

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.580
That may be the case.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.500
There's a shop like that in
South Straug, after all...

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:51.920
At any rate, thanks to that,

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:56.130
folks decided there wasn't any profit there
and stopped hunting them.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.380
So that's what happened...?

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:03.420
Ms. Sarasa, just what sort of creatures
are frostfang bats anyway?

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.330
I'd like to hear more details too.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:06.380
Indeed.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:07.750
Well, to put it simply...

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:12.670
Their most notable feature are the fangs
that give them their name.

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:17.080
They can freeze a target by biting them.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:20.830
That said, they don't tend to
attack people or animals.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:23.580
Generally, they freeze fruits instead.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:28.580
They use that preserved food to hole up
in caves and make it through winter.

00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:31.750
So, they're good targets
because they aren't ferocious?

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:34.790
If you want, shall I provide an on-site lecture?

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:37.080
You'd do that, Ms. Owner...?

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.460
I want their fangs, after all.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:42.330
Could I ask you to watch the shop, Lorea?

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:43.830
Of course!

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:47.380
Mr. Andre, could you guide us to the cave?

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.250
We can split the fangs we gather evenly!

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:53.960
That'd benefit us too,
so I certainly won't complain...

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:57.750
But wouldn't it be dangerous for you to...

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:01.040
Nah, of course not.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:08.210
Sorry, I let your appearance influence me there.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:12.750
Huh?! D-do I really look that much
like I can't fight?!

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.420
Sure do!

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:30.880
So, these are the northern caves, are they...?

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:33.830
We haven't even stepped inside yet,
and it's already gotten plenty chilly.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:36.380
Yes, they're definitely here.

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:38.830
The issue is whether or not
we can hunt them down properly...

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:40.380
Don't worry.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:44.710
Once you hunt enough of them,
the frostfang bats will prioritize getting away.

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:49.250
But if you try to corner them
and wipe them all out...

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:53.210
The whole swarm of them will
come after you like mad.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:57.330
Lots of people have been frozen
and died that way.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.380
Still, I don't think we have to worry
about that with this group!

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.790
H-huh...?

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.500
That stinks!

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:20.540
Sure does.

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.130
What's with the stench?

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:27.380
Ah, frostfang bats generally
hang down from the cave ceiling.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:30.040
And so, all sorts of stuff falls on down.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:31.920
Like what?

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:34.500
Er, all sorts of stuff...

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:37.500
Wait, are you saying this is...

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:40.500
Yes...

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:45.000
Ms. Owner, we didn't bring along umbrellas!

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.460
Don't worry.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:51.170
I'll keep us safe with my air wall magic.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:55.790
Wait, are you seriously okay
with this stench, Ms. Owner?

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:59.670
A lot of ingredients with powerful scents
are used in alchemy, after all.

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:02.880
I'm using a potion to help
reduce the bad smells.

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:06.420
Sniff, sniff...

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:10.170
The stench isn't entirely gone,
but this is far better.

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:11.750
It's completely different now!

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:15.380
It's a potion meant to block
more smell than usual.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:18.830
It would be dangerous to
block it completely, after all.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.080
Take care.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:25.040
The ground is frozen around here.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.880
Better that than coated in droppings.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.380
Look up above.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:35.000
There they are...

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:36.330
Air wall!

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:40.670
So, how should we get started?

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:46.250
The value of frostfang bat fangs changes
based on their ability to freeze.

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:50.670
Put simply, ones under the age of five
aren't worth much.

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:52.790
How can you tell them apart?

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:55.000
There are a number of methods.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:57.880
Normally in a cave like this,

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:01.790
the further in you go the older
and larger they become.

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:05.790
In other words, we want to hunt them
as far in as we can.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:06.830
Right!

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:07.920
Also...

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:15.040
After you actually hunt one,
there are methods for telling them apart.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:19.580
To start, you have the color of their fangs.

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:22.960
The deeper blue, the older they are.

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:24.630
Ah, what a beautiful color...

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:26.330
This is still on the lighter side.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.290
After the age of ten
they're an even prettier deep blue.

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:31.710
To tell even more precisely
you can look here at the root.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:35.130
There are lines.
So the number of those tells their age?

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:36.330
That's right.

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:39.000
There are five here, so it'd be six years old.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:40.250
I see.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:42.790
Then there's the freezing ability.

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:46.580
If it's so cold that you soon have to stop
after touching it with your bare hand,

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.290
then it should be plenty valuable.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.000
Oh, I see.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:52.040
Well then, let's go ahead and confirm.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:57.630
Ms. Owner, why are you teasing me so?

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:59.500
Well, you see...

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:02.380
If you happen to cut your finger
on one of these fangs,

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:05.170
it would freeze over in seconds...

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:09.670
Ow...

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:11.710
Geez...

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:17.670
Ms. Iris!

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:23.790
Th-this is dangerous, but I just can't stop!

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:25.830
Watch out!

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:27.040
Gotcha!

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:28.630
There! Oh no!

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:29.710
Iris!

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:30.790
Everybody!

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:37.250
No way! I'm slipping!

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:43.630
We finally stopped...

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:45.080
Iris!

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:46.710
Shh!

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:09.290
Ms. Owner, those look quite large.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:11.540
They're certainly big enough.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.710
We could go even further in,
but let's get to work here.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.250
Air wall!

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.380
Stay on guard.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.130
This place is full of crap too.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:22.670
The two of us are up first, Ms. Kate.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:27.540
It'll be a hassle if they start making a fuss,
so aim to take them out in one shot.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:29.210
That's not so simple.

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:31.420
If the frostfang bats start flying around,

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:34.130
then it'll be time for the swords and spears.

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:35.210
Understood.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:36.460
Leave it to us.

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:38.830
Well then, let's get started!

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.290
Good job, Kate!

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:51.750
Ah, sorry!

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.830
No worries. Step back, Ms. Kate!

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.330
Now, everyone!

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:58.330
Right!

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.080
Air wall, tightened!

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:02.670
Take that!

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:06.880
Perfect! Keep it up!

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:12.170
We somehow made it through...

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:15.330
Let's go ahead and collect the fangs here.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:17.830
Do we just break them off?

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:21.630
Yes, they'll come loose easily
if you pull at the base.

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.830
Make sure you're wearing
leather gloves, though.

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:26.750
Assuming you don't want to
lose a finger, that is.

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:29.380
O-of course I will.

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:33.830
You sure work quickly, Sarasa.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:37.080
Aren't you scared of cutting yourself
with those thin gloves?

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.250
These are artifacts
known as flexible gloves.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:43.500
They're sturdy enough that sharp edges
won't cut through them so easily.

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:46.630
Ooh, mind if I give them a bit of a try?

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:47.630
Go ahead!

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:52.210
Ooh, these are amazing!

00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:56.210
The downside is that it uses
a bit of magical power to wear them.

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:59.080
Yeah, but I can't even feel it.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:02.790
These are so thin, but they can even
guard against frostfang bat fangs.

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:04.750
By the way, what do they cost?

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:06.670
3,800 rhea!

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:11.170
At that price, it's certainly worth
considering for the sense of security.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:14.380
If you buy in bulk,
I can also give a discount!

00:14:14.380 --> 00:14:15.500
Alright!

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.750
I'll talk to the other gatherers
I know about it!

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:19.330
Thank you!

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:23.290
Well then, let's split everything up equally.

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:25.580
You really don't mind, Sarasa?

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:28.290
Splitting things equally with us, I mean.

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:32.210
No matter how you look at it,
you definitely played the biggest role.

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:35.380
I said I'd split it evenly in exchange for
you showing us the way, right?

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:38.040
Really? Still, I feel bad about it...

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:41.670
We'll discuss the matter of your
repayment later, Ms. Iris and Ms. Kate.

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:45.380
I don't want you to get hurt because
I put too much pressure on you.

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:47.250
Thanks, Ms. Owner.

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:48.790
We owe you greatly.

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:53.960
Ah, no. If you two die, then you won't
be able to pay me back, after all.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:56.880
That's true...

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:00.500
Now then, let's split this all up
and hurry on back!

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:01.630
Yeah!

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:06.920
All finished!

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:10.500
That should be good enough for today.

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:15.080
It ended up taking till morning...

00:15:16.710 --> 00:15:18.130
Ms. Sarasa?

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:19.290
Yes?

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:21.960
Good morning!

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:23.540
Did you stay up all night again...?

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:25.750
Yeah, for the new products.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.500
Wow, such cute hats!

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:31.080
I figured the villagers could
make use of these too...

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:32.670
Go ahead and try one on.

00:15:32.670 --> 00:15:34.580
Huh?! Is it really alright?!

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:35.710
Of course!

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:40.170
It's nice and cool!

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:42.380
It's called a cooling hat.

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:45.170
Since it cools off your head
and upper body,

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.460
I figured it'd be good for
working during the day.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:48.750
Amazing!

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:51.500
Did you use the frostfang bat fangs
for these too?

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:53.830
Yeah. I figured since we had them,

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:57.290
I should make something with them
besides just the cooling core.

00:15:57.290 --> 00:15:59.420
This is perfect!

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:01.830
So, what about those?

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:04.540
Ah, those are flexible gloves.

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:07.210
Mr. Andre seemed like he was
going to place an order,

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:09.420
so I hurried up and made them.

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:11.170
As impressive as always.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:13.920
But make sure you get proper sleep tonight.

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:17.500
R-right...

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:23.420
Hey there, Lorea.

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:25.460
Ah, Mr. Andre!

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:26.710
Hey!

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:29.960
Here's the order for the gloves.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:31.420
I got it all put together.

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:33.670
Huh?! You handled that already?

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:35.420
Without even seeing the final products?

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:38.710
That's because everyone trusts you, Sarasa.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:41.330
I'm certainly glad to hear it.

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:46.170
Alchemists can't keep things going
if they lose the trust of gatherers.

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:49.380
You're a great saleswoman, Sarasa.

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:53.710
You've got perfect timing when it
comes to showing off your wares.

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:55.880
I'll hurry up and get them made!

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:57.170
Ah, right.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:59.420
I also brought these.

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:04.540
Oh, spite worms...

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:07.040
There should be around thirty in there.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.290
Yes, and they're in good shape!

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:10.880
Thank you!

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:14.750
You're so strong, Lorea...

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:20.130
I closed up shop, Ms. Sarasa!

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:21.040
Huh?!

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:24.670
Wh-what's going on here?!

00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:26.290
Ah, Lorea.

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:30.670
You have to dry flexible gloves
like this to finish them off.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:32.750
I-I see...

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:35.920
Good work again today.
How did things go with the shop?

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:37.130
Ah, right!

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:40.290
The insect repellant veils
are selling really well!

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:44.630
And the new product, the cooling hats,
got a great reaction too!

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:47.710
It really was a good idea to make
those models, wasn't it?

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.960
I get the feeling that they'll be popular sellers!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.250
Alright, in that case,

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:55.330
maybe it's time for the next step...

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:56.540
The next step?

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:59.460
Yeah! We're not just working on
the shop, after all!

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:02.210
Mr. Geberk!

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:05.170
What's with that unsettling sight...?

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:09.420
Yeah, it's a perfect fit.

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:11.170
Great work as always, Mr. Geberk!

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:14.290
Wow! This is my first time
ever seeing a refrigerator!

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:16.710
I hardly ever make them my...

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:21.830
What's that about?!

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:28.210
So, you already wish to discuss
what to do next?

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:31.210
Running a business certainly sounds difficult...

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:34.880
Actually, I wanted to discuss
something a bit different.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:38.420
Things seem to have settled down
with the shop a bit, but...

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:42.920
I've become an alchemist, and come here to
this village and formed ties with everyone.

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:47.670
With my shop, I... I want to help everyone
in the village live even better lives.

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:51.380
So, could you help me
think on how to do that?

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:52.920
Everyone in the village...

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:55.580
How splendid, Ms. Owner.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:57.040
Ms. Sarasa...

00:18:57.040 --> 00:19:00.130
Ah, no, that's just something I repeated...

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:01.540
Even still!

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:06.250
To start, with, I'd like to increase
the amount of money

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:08.420
circulating throughout the village...

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:10.500
Money, is it...?

00:19:10.880 --> 00:19:14.920
It's true that you don't need much
in order to live here.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:18.830
We only ever tend to spend money
at the general store at most.

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:23.330
Aside from gatherers, most folks
seem to tend to barter instead.

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:25.000
That's true...

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:26.960
Hmm...

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:31.630
It's a fine idea, but now that we've
turned to economic matters...

00:19:31.630 --> 00:19:34.460
Well, that's not so easy to handle.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:36.750
Since it's come to this...

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:40.040
I'll offer a somewhat expensive cookie
I bought in South Straug

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:42.920
to anyone who comes up with a good idea!

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:46.330
I-is the greatest issue not

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:50.000
that there is little work that pays
to be had here in the village?

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:54.080
That's why they've established a lifestyle
where you don't need money...

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.880
There's not any money
to begin with in the village.

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:59.960
In other words, increasing the
amount of money circulating

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:03.750
means finding someone to
sell to outside the village!

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:06.920
That's true! I think you might just be right!

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:13.710
Th-the only ones bringing in money from outside
are yourself and we gatherers, correct?

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:18.040
Then what about if you
hire the villagers, Ms. Owner?

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:20.380
So, I could be a source of work...?

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:21.580
That's a great idea!

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:22.960
Hooray!

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:25.880
Whoa, the ideas started flowing
as soon as the sweets came out!

00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:29.080
But the only ones you can
really order work from

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:32.130
are Mr. Geberk and Mr. Gizdo, right...?

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:33.960
That's certainly true.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:35.080
Hooray!

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:37.670
Ms. Owner, that was just a simple question!

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:40.040
Yeah, but Lorea's just so cute!

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:40.920
Wha?!

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.790
What about gathering medicinal herbs?

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:46.460
I would need to ask someone who
specializes in such things.

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:49.580
So, you couldn't ask an amateur to
do it in their spare time, huh...?

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:51.670
Ah, now that I think of it,

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:55.080
you've been making the hat portions
of the cooling hats yourself, right?

00:20:56.040 --> 00:21:00.250
I see! Before I attach the cooling function,
they're just ordinary hats!

00:21:00.250 --> 00:21:02.630
That doesn't need any alchemy,
so I could hire someone to handle that!

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:06.290
But once I sell enough of the coolings hats,

00:21:06.290 --> 00:21:09.330
I'll eventually hit a maximum limit on sales...

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:12.000
Then why not look at external sales?

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.040
External sales?

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:14.290
That's right!

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:16.710
You can sell your goods in other towns!

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:20.000
We could ask my dad to help go sell them too!

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:22.130
That could work...!

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:25.960
In that case, you'll need appealing
designs for selling in town!

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:29.670
I'll make some references!
Like illustrations and the like!

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.670
I'll help out too.

00:21:31.670 --> 00:21:34.380
This'll work! I'm just sure of it!

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:36.920
You've given me so many great ideas...!

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:42.000
Go ahead and eat as many as you want!

00:21:42.290 --> 00:21:43.880
Hooray!

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:48.670
You wish to have the villagers
help with your products?

00:21:48.670 --> 00:21:49.580
That's right.

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:51.210
I would commission them.

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:55.920
To start, the villagers could make the hats
on their own and set prices for them.

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:59.380
Then I would add cooling functions to them

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:02.080
and add an additional fee on top of
the cost set by the villagers,

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:03.710
then sell them in my shop.

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:10.880
But in that case, we wouldn't get paid
if the hats don't sell.

00:22:10.880 --> 00:22:13.540
This won't end in losses
for the villagers, will it...?

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:15.630
That's not the case at all, Father.

00:22:16.710 --> 00:22:20.960
Sarasa's really thinking about
the village with this proposal.

00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:22.460
What do you mean?

00:22:22.630 --> 00:22:26.920
Sarasa's the one who shoulders a lot of
the cost of making the cooling hats.

00:22:26.920 --> 00:22:28.710
If they don't sell,

00:22:28.710 --> 00:22:32.210
she'll suffer a lot more serious losses
than just the cost of the base hats.

00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:35.000
And she's come here saying
she's willing to take that risk.

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:36.710
But Father, you...

00:22:36.710 --> 00:22:37.960
I see...

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:41.170
If that's what you have to say on the matter,
Elyn, I'm sure you must be right.

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:44.880
Could I ask you to do this for
the village's sake, Sarasa?

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:46.080
Of course!

00:22:55.500 --> 00:22:57.460
Ms. Sarasa!

00:22:57.670 --> 00:22:59.460
Look!

00:22:59.790 --> 00:23:03.420
I heard what some gatherers had to say,
and we made this helm!

00:23:03.630 --> 00:23:05.500
You made that, Lorea?

00:23:05.500 --> 00:23:07.130
No, my great grandmother!

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:11.670
She usually doesn't move all that much,
but this got her really fired up!

00:23:11.670 --> 00:23:14.830
Everyone in the village is helping out!

00:23:16.460 --> 00:23:17.880
Thanks!

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.040
Alright!

00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:30.580
The plan to make cooling hats
a Yok Village specialty...

00:23:30.920 --> 00:23:32.880
is a go!

